From a527295159bed68c32a1f5c67ae4613a3019e2b3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Mon, 29 Jun 2026 19:07:14 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 04910/11362] [outer-loop] ARC: frame_change_prune validation
 -> DO NOT ENABLE (regresses, no gain)

Validated the operator-requested frame_change_prune_threshold enable against the
solve-rate-no-regression gate. Combined evidence:
- exp4511 (live solve-rate A/B, full sweep 0.25-0.75): regresses solve-rate 4->3,
  NO efficiency gain (median actions 7760->7766). positive control passed.
- winpath test (this, 21 games): every winning-path action scores >=0.935, so NONE
  would be pruned at any T up to 0.9. The exp4511 regression is therefore exploration-
  DISCOVERY divergence (pruning no-op candidates the explorer must traverse to DISCOVER
  the path), not winning-action pruning -- invisible to static held-out precision.
Gate FAILS -> config NOT changed (frame_change_prune_threshold stays None).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
